IMPORT `nii-s238-housewife`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: s 238 "עקרת בית", "אלמנה", "אלמנה בת קצבה". Row IL-33.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew (lines 2403-2405, 2428-2429) before the run.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures`

avi MEANS `an Israeli employee` "Avi" `born` (YMD 1988 3 10) `who is` `male`
batya MEANS `a person` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 6 20)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`
batyaS MEANS `a person` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 6 20)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`

GIVEN s IS A `Marital status`
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A woman's marriage`
`a marriage:` s `, traces vanished:` a `, abroad against her will:` b MEANS
    `A woman's marriage` WITH
        `marital status`                                                                                      IS s
        `her spouse's traces have vanished for two years`                                                     IS a
        `her spouse has been abroad for two years without her consent and has not supported her in that time` IS b

-- Dina: a woman born 1 January 1970, not working.
dina MEANS `a person` "Dina" `born` (YMD 1970 1 1) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1970 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`

married MEANS `a marriage:` `married` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE

GIVEN married IS A DATE
      death   IS A DATE
      child   IS A BOOLEAN
      sep     IS A BOOLEAN
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      borne   IS A BOOLEAN
      supp    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A widowing`
`a widowing: married` married `, died` death `, child` child `, separated` sep `, entitled to maintenance` entitled `, he bore her maintenance` borne `, supplement paid` supp MEANS
    `A widowing` WITH
        `she was his wife at his death`                                                                  IS TRUE
        `the day of the marriage`                                                                        IS married
        `the day of his death`                                                                           IS death
        `she bore him a child`                                                                           IS child
        `in the five years before his death she was separated from him for three years or more, including the twelve months before his death` IS sep
        `she was entitled to maintenance from him by a judgment or a written agreement`                  IS entitled
        `he did in fact bear her maintenance in the twelve months before his death`                      IS borne
        `a dependants' supplement was paid for her at his death under section 200 or 244`                IS supp

§ `Tests — a housewife`

§§ `The ordinary case`

-- Batya: a woman, not an employee, not self-employed, married, not an agunah; her spouse Avi is a resident
-- of 37 insured under Chapter 11. A housewife.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§§ `Each condition alone defeats it`

-- An employee: she works.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` (batyaS `with the work` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- Self-employed: she works on her own account.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` (batyaS `with the work` `the work of a self-employed person in Israel`) `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- Not married: never married, divorced, widowed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `never married` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `divorced` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `widowed` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- An agunah: the spouse's traces vanished two years ago, or he has been abroad against her will two years and
-- has not supported her.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `married` `, traces vanished:` TRUE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `married` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` TRUE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A spouse not insured under Chapter 11: a visitor (not a resident); a man who first became a resident at
-- his 62nd birthday (Part C), born 1 January 1950, resident from 1 January 2012.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`)) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST (`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`)) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A man is not a housewife; the chain stops at the first condition, so no record of a spouse is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A working woman is not one, whatever her spouse.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` (batyaS `with the work` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- No record of the spouse of a married woman who does not work: declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§§ `A woman known in public as a wife (fork H1)`

-- s 238 says "אשה נשואה" (a married woman); s 1 "אשתו" includes a woman known in public as his wife who
-- lives with him. Batya, not married, known in public as Avi's wife, who is insured: on the narrow reading
-- she is not a housewife; on the wide reading she is; by default the text does not decide.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `known in public as the wife of a man and living with him, without being married to him` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `known in public as the wife of a man and living with him, without being married to him` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the word married in the definition of a housewife` `read as` `married means married only`)
#ASSERT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `known in public as the wife of a man and living with him, without being married to him` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the word married in the definition of a housewife` `read as` `married includes a woman known in public as the wife and living with him`)
-- Where she works, both readings agree (not a housewife), so the default answers.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a housewife:` (batyaS `with the work` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `, her marriage` (`a marriage:` `known in public as the wife of a man and living with him, without being married to him` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE) `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- For a married woman the reading is not in play, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a housewife:` batyaS `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§ `Tests — a widow ("אלמנה")`

-- Dates: the marriage on the first, the death on the second.
-- W1 a wife of five years who bore a child, no separation: a widow.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- W2 a marriage of less than a year without a child (1 January to 31 December 2025): not a widow ...
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- ... one year to the day (1 January 2025 to 1 January 2026): "less than a year" no longer holds: a widow.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- ... or if she bore him a child, even in the short marriage.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- W3 a woman of 55 or over at the death: the period is half a year. Born 1 January 1970, 55 on 1 January 2025.
--   Married 1 June 2024, died 1 January 2025: seven months, she is 55: not less than half a year: a widow.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` dina `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2024 6 1) `, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
--   Married 1 June 2024, died 31 December 2024 (she is 54): the year applies; seven months is less than a year
--   and she bore no child: not a widow.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` dina `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2024 6 1) `, died` (YMD 2024 12 31) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
--   Aged 55, married 1 August 2024, died 1 January 2025: five months, less than half a year: not a widow.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` dina `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2024 8 1) `, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- W4 paragraph (2). Separated three years of the five including the last twelve months (sep), not entitled
-- to maintenance (entitled FALSE), and he did bear her maintenance (borne TRUE): inside the condition she
-- is excluded: not a widow, on both readings.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` TRUE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Separated, entitled to maintenance and he bore it: not excluded on either reading: a widow.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` TRUE `, entitled to maintenance` TRUE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Separated, entitled, but he did not in fact bear it: inside: excluded; whole: excluded (¬borne).
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` TRUE `, entitled to maintenance` TRUE `, he bore her maintenance` FALSE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Not separated and he did not in fact bear her maintenance: inside the condition of separation she is not
-- excluded; as an alternative to the whole she is. The text does not say which: declined by default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` TRUE `, he bore her maintenance` FALSE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` TRUE `, he bore her maintenance` FALSE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow` `read as` `the maintenance limbs are alternatives inside the condition of separation`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` TRUE `, he bore her maintenance` FALSE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow` `read as` `the lack of actual maintenance is an alternative to the whole of the separation condition`)
-- A woman for whom a dependants' supplement was paid at the death: paragraph (2) does not apply to her.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` TRUE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` FALSE `, supplement paid` TRUE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- W5 she was not his wife at his death.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow:` batyaS `, widowed` (`A widowing` WITH `she was his wife at his death` IS FALSE, `the day of the marriage` IS YMD 2010 1 1, `the day of his death` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `she bore him a child` IS TRUE, `in the five years before his death she was separated from him for three years or more, including the twelve months before his death` IS FALSE, `she was entitled to maintenance from him by a judgment or a written agreement` IS FALSE, `he did in fact bear her maintenance in the twelve months before his death` IS TRUE, `a dependants' supplement was paid for her at his death under section 200 or 244` IS FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — a widow pensioner ("אלמנה בת קצבה")`

-- A widow who is not an employee and not self-employed and is entitled to a pension under s 132(1) to (5) or
-- s 252. Entitlement to those pensions is a fact the Institute records (NOTES.md): ss 132 and 252 are not
-- encoded.
#ASSERT `s 238 — a widow pensioner:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, her pension` (`A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS TRUE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Not entitled to the pension.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow pensioner:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, her pension` (`A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- An employee widow is not a widow pensioner.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow pensioner:` (batyaS `with the work` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, her pension` (`A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS TRUE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- A pension but a short marriage without a child: not a widow, so not a widow pensioner.
#ASSERT NOT `s 238 — a widow pensioner:` batyaS `, widowed` (`a widowing: married` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, child` FALSE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled to maintenance` FALSE `, he bore her maintenance` TRUE `, supplement paid` FALSE) `, her pension` (`A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS TRUE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
